{
"@type":"Question",
"name":"What is a SEG light box?",
"acceptedAnswer":{
"@type":"Answer",
"text":"A SEG light box is an illuminated display system that uses silicone edge graphics inserted into an aluminum frame. LED lighting creates a seamless, bright and professional backlit display for exhibitions, trade shows and brand events."
}
},


{
"@type":"Question",
"name":"What does SEG stand for in exhibition displays?",
"acceptedAnswer":{
"@type":"Answer",
"text":"SEG stands for Silicone Edge Graphics. The fabric graphic has a silicone strip sewn around the edge, allowing it to be inserted into an aluminum frame channel for a smooth and wrinkle-free appearance."
}
},


{
"@type":"Question",
"name":"What are the advantages of SEG light boxes?",
"acceptedAnswer":{
"@type":"Answer",
"text":"SEG light boxes provide seamless graphics, bright LED illumination, professional appearance, easy installation, reusable frames and replaceable fabric graphics."
}
},


{
"@type":"Question",
"name":"How is a SEG light box different from a traditional banner display?",
"acceptedAnswer":{
"@type":"Answer",
"text":"Unlike traditional banner displays, SEG light boxes use illuminated fabric graphics and aluminum frames to create a premium three-dimensional visual experience with stronger brand impact."
}
},


